column307:
17/Dec/25 2:29 PM;zpryor;For pressures, it has been reduced to just the differential pressures that will be displayed on the control screens as that is really what the operators are reacting to and avoids them having to do mental math. This also reduces the screen clutter that including all pressures brings and focuses the attention on what actual is important

Equalized by Timing method will be a pop up if that is how we were equalized

The requirements need to be updated to reflect this;;;

column305:
10/Dec/25 12:39 PM;zpryor;All of the time tracked to this item not just is for the time spent to provide a response but also includes time needed to review what a Kalman filter is that the NAVSEA representative suggested the TCS could utilize to calculated average liquid level in Tube 9 and review the current process by which the TCS plans to calculated liquid level in Tube 9 which involves a low pass filter.

The TCS plans to calculate liquid level by correcting the SAPT measurements by translating to the center of the tube to negate water slosh from pitch and roll, taking the average or median of the upper and lower sensor values, filtering out the noise through a low pass filter, and then through a differential pressure calculation between the filtered upper and lower pressures calculate an accurate liquid level through a hydrostatic pressure equation based on the static water head indicated by the differential pressure value. That instantaneous liquid level can then be averaged over a specified time interval to sufficiently track the change in Tube 9 liquid level the TCS needs to react.

 

 ;;;

